      "body": "## Overview\n\nFixes #61874. Return HTTP 400 (`BadRequestError`) instead of HTTP 500 when local media is requested without `--allowed-local-media-path`.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Changes the disabled local media exception in `MediaConnector._load_file_url` from `RuntimeError` to `ValueError`.\n- `create_error_response` correctly maps `ValueError` to HTTP 400 `BadRequestError`, preserving the security denial message while correctly categorizing it as a client error rather than an internal server error.\n- Updates existing unit tests in `test_connector.py` and adds sync/async regression tests in `test_unprocessable_entity_error.py`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Verified locally that requesting `file:///...` without `--allowed-local-media-path` raises `ValueError` and produces:\n  `code: 400`, `type: BadRequestError`, `message: \"Cannot load local files without \\`--allowed-local-media-path\\`.\"`.\n- Formatted and validated with `ruff format --check` and `ruff check`.\n\n## Details\n\nWhen `--allowed-local-media-path` is omitted, `MediaConnector.allowed_local_media_path` is `None`. Previously, `_load_file_url` raised a bare `RuntimeError`. When handled by `create_error_response`, unmapped `RuntimeError` instances default to `InternalServerError` (HTTP 500).\n\nIn contrast, other client-side URL validation rejections in `MediaConnector` (such as accessing files outside the allowed subpath, disallowed media domains, or unsupported schemes) raise `ValueError`, which maps to HTTP 400. Aligning the disabled local media check with `ValueError` ensures correct HTTP 400 status reporting across both sync and async request pipelines.\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
